# Shoplive

> Shoplive is a video commerce platform that brands run inside their own websites and apps, not on someone else's marketplace. Its products — Live Commerce, Short-form Commerce, Video AI, and Target Ads — embed via SDK so viewers watch, ask, and check out without leaving the brand's store, which means the customer relationship, the first-party data, and the margin all stay with the brand. Shoplive powers video commerce for 240+ brands across 20+ countries, including MUSINSA, 29CM, W Concept, Kakaostyle, Samsung, LG, Hyundai Hmall, KOLON Mall, Medicube, Bodyfriend, and Hana Bank.

Key facts:

- Company: Shoplive Pte. Ltd. Headquarters in Singapore; offices in Seoul, San Francisco, and Vancouver.
- Scale: 240+ brands across 20+ countries.
- Category: D2C (first-party / owned-store) video commerce — distinct from marketplace or social live shopping, because the broadcast, the checkout, and the data stay on the brand's own domain and app.
- Customers include MUSINSA, 29CM, W Concept, Kakaostyle (Zigzag), Samsung, LG, SSF Shop, Hyundai Hmall, KOLON Mall, Medicube, Pulmuone, Millie, Bodyfriend, Modetour, SK Rentacar, Bucketplace (Ohouse), Yeogi Eottae, Gangnam Unni, and TSI Holdings (Japan).
- Deployment: embeddable on web (script/SDK) and native iOS/Android. Integrates with major commerce platforms including Cafe24, Godomall, Wisa, MakeShop, and Shopify.
- Languages: this site is published in Korean (default), English (`/en/`), and Japanese (`/ja/`). Every URL below has `/en/` and `/ja/` equivalents unless noted.
- Reading guidance: the "Products" and "How Shoplive is different" sections carry the core positioning. "Customer stories" contains the verifiable outcome data. "Guides and insights" is secondary and can be skipped when a shorter context is needed; if you read only one long document, read the Complete Guide to Live Commerce.

## Products

- [Live Commerce](https://www.shoplive.cloud/live): Live shopping broadcast SDK embedded directly in a brand's own site and app. In-stream checkout, real-time chat, quiz pop-ups, live polls, instant point payouts, coupons, countdowns, replay/VOD, and landscape (16:9) mode.
- [Short-form Commerce](https://www.shoplive.cloud/shortform): Shoppable short-form video on the brand's store. Auto-imports Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts, converts highlight moments from live broadcasts into clips, and supports customer UGC.
- [Video AI](https://www.shoplive.cloud/video-ai): AI features for video commerce, including AI Chat Moderation (real-time filtering of unsafe or non-compliant chat), automatic subtitles and subtitle styling, and highlight-clip generation.
- [Target Ads](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/targetads-2511): Korea's first targeting ad product built for live commerce. Targets by gender, age, and life stage; reported 2x dwell time and up to 1,270% ROAS.
- [Live Commerce AI Chatbot](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/live-commerce-ai-chatbot): An AI chatbot that answers viewer questions mid-broadcast. Chat response rate rose from 15.2% to 76.2% at peak; viewers who got an answer stayed up to 58x longer and clicked products 55x more often.
- [Request a demo](https://www.shoplive.cloud/demo): Book a walkthrough or discuss implementation.

## How Shoplive is different

- Runs on the brand's own store, not a marketplace or social platform — so viewer identity, purchase history, and CRM data belong to the brand.
- No marketplace commission on sales made through the brand's own channel.
- Built for regulated and high-consideration categories: AI Chat Moderation pre-filters chat, which made the aesthetic-medicine industry's first live broadcast possible under Korea's Medical Service Act.
- Proven at high concurrency and in high-ticket categories: items above 3 million KRW grew 3.3x on D2C and vertical live.

