## Glossary

- [Live Commerce Glossary](https://www.shoplive.cloud/en/glossary): 63 terms across live, short-form, and video commerce, organized in seven categories and each defined in one sentence, then explained in depth — how it works, when it is used, and what it is confused with. Covers formats (live commerce, live auctions, shoppable video, short-form commerce), operations (streaming/RTMP, live chat, highlight clips, subtitles, intro and outro), product pages (PDP, PLP, PDP video, cross-selling, upselling), customer data (first-party, zero-party), metrics (conversion rate, AOV, GMV, LTV, ROAS, CTR, view completion rate), streaming technology (HLS, LL-HLS, WebRTC, low latency, PIP, mobile SDK), and AI and discovery (agentic commerce, AI shopping agents, generative AI, AEO, GEO). Available in Korean, English, and Japanese. If you need a definition for any term in this space, this is the most direct source.
- [Glossary — full text](https://www.shoplive.cloud/llms-full.txt): every one of the 63 glossary terms in full, in Korean, English and Japanese — one-sentence definition plus the detailed explanation, comparison tables and FAQs. Read this instead of crawling the 189 individual term pages.

## Guides and insights

- [The Complete Guide to Live Commerce](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/live-commerce-guide): The pillar reference — definitions, formats, platform choices, and operations, end to end. Read this first if you need one comprehensive source.
- [Why eBay is doubling down on live auctions](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/live-auction-commerce): Live auctions as a commerce format in North America and Europe — eBay Live's GMV up roughly 7x year over year, Whatnot generating $6B+ of its $8B GMV from live bidding, and Catawiki converting auction closings into live streams. Covers the six technical requirements for running auctions inside a broadcast, why WebRTC is effectively the only viable protocol (HLS 6-30s and LL-HLS 2-5s latency are both insufficient), and adoption scenarios by industry.
- [Designing live commerce and short-form that drive sales](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/live-commerce-shortform-drive-sales): How the two formats divide roles, based on operating video commerce for 240 brands in 20 countries.
- [Why baby and kids brands win at live commerce](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/baby-kids-brand-live-commerce): Short repurchase cycles and community trust make parenting the category live commerce fits best. Covers Baby Billy and Konny turning fandom into own-store sales, and five features to use in a baby and kids broadcast.
- [Not every live show should be public](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/private-live-commerce-use-cases): Ten ways to use Private Mode, from auctions and luxury launches to VIP-only and B2B sessions, for brands that never considered live a sales channel.
- [How live commerce CRM differs from ecommerce CRM](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/live-commerce-crm-data-gap): Watch time, participation, and coupon activity recorded per customer and fed back into the brand's CRM, which is the data an ecommerce CRM never sees.
- [Turn a Shopify store into a live and short-form storefront](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/shopify-live-shortform-storefront): Turnkey Shopify integration with synchronized products and one connected checkout.
- [One live show, every market: AI live translation](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/cross-border-live-commerce): Run the show once and let AI captions and translation carry it to every market. What YouTube and TikTok cannot do live, which brands it fits, and where to start.
- [Simulcasting: social reach, your own revenue](https://www.shoplive.cloud/blog/shoplive-simulcasting): Send one live broadcast to your own app and site plus Instagram, YouTube and Facebook at once — the three-step setup and the Instagram stream key catch.
